WEBVTT

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:11.080
<i>This is where a man became a legend.</i>

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.400
<i>Faced with overwhelming odds,</i>

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.410
<i>he struggled, struggled,</i>

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:16.910
<i>and struggled...</i>

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:18.910
<i>He fell countless times,</i>

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.410
<i>only to climb his way back up!</i>

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:25.330
<i>And in spite of never-ending struggles, 
he pushed forward.</i>

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:28.420
<i>The legendary pariah...</i>

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:33.880
<i>His name is Itou Kaiji!</i>

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.680
<b>Itou Kaiji</b>

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.390
<i>Kaiji: a man who had an average 
and indulgent lifestyle,</i>

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.020
<i>until he was forced to 
shoulder a sizable debt,</i>

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:48.310
<i>and was then lured into pursuing 
the ultimate means of</i>

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.110
<b>Endou Financing</b>

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:51.110
<i>repaying it by his debt collector, Endou!</i>

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:50.110
<b>Loan Agreement</b>

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:52.610
<i>That was...</i>

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:54.320
<b>Psst...</b>

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.780
<i>the luxury liner of hope, </i>Espoir<i>!</i>

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.780
<b>Espoir</b>

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:02.290
<i>Gathered onboard are losers 
similar to Kaiji.</i>

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.130
<i>A mob of scum!</i>

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.860
<i>All guests for a one-night cruise!</i>

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:08.880
<i>And so begins the legend!</i>

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.960
<i>The men engage in a contest known as...</i>

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.180
<b>Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors</b>

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.250
<i>Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors!</i>

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:21.220
<i>At a glance, it looks like 
a simple game of chance.</i>

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:27.560
<i>But thanks to prodigious inspiration 
and sharp observation, he survives!</i>

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:31.400
<b>Starside Hotel</b>

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:31.400
<i>Another trial awaits...</i>

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.430
<i>A hell harsher than even the </i>Espoir<i>:</i>

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.660
<i>The Brave Men Road!</i>

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:40.990
<b>Brave Men Road</b>

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.480
<i>A chilling game that 
puts him head-to-head</i>

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.450
<i>with death by crossing an iron beam!</i>

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:49.170
<i>One wrong step, and it's a long way down!</i>

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:56.260
<i>But Kaiji manages to be the sole survivor!</i>

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:00.180
<i>Destiny calls him to the 
table of yet another game...</i>

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:10.480
<i>Waiting for him is the president of 
the Teiai Group, Hyoudou Kazutaka!</i>

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:15.690
<b>Hyoudou Kazutaka</b>

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.950
<i>A monster that reigns over the underworld!</i>

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:21.700
<i>And acting as Hyoudou's agent is this man...</i>

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:25.770
<i>Tonegawa Yukio!</i>

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.960
<b>Tonegawa Yukio</b>

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:31.020
<i>All-encompassing powers of observation.</i>

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.420
<i>Demonic mental fortitude.</i>

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:37.550
<i>The Teiai Group's number-two man!</i>

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.890
<i>Tonegawa completely dominates Kaiji.</i>

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:47.850
<b>E-Card</b>

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:46.560
<i>He never gives the slightest opening.</i>

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.740
<i>Everything plays out one-sidedly, 
exactly as he plans.</i>

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:55.690
<i>However, he's so sharp...
that he ends up cutting himself.</i>

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:58.190
Thank you...

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:02.200
for being exceptional.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.080
<i>An unthinkable loss.</i>

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:12.090
<i>The president was furious!</i>

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:17.090
<i>Tonegawa is laid low because 
of how exceptional he is.</i>

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:20.840
<i>He's forced to risk his own flesh to atone 
in the most agonizing way imaginable!</i>

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.850
<i>That was...</i>

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:27.880
<i>the Roasting Kneeling!</i>

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:28.910
<b>Roasting Kneeling</b>

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:36.330
<i>Yes, this man is the legendary foil of 
the legendary Itou Kaiji, Tonegawa Yukio!</i>

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:45.490
<i>Our story begins before Tonegawa 
ever encountered Kaiji.</i>

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.170
So he finally flew the coop...

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:52.850
Agenda 01
<b>Initiative</b>

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:49.930
He sure gave us a lot of trouble.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:53.290
If he was going to skip town, 
he should've just paid his debt on time.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:58.190
I'd guess the whole family is up in 
the mountains or in the Sea of Japan.

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:00.170
And either way...

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.720
Well, on to the next one.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:12.390
Chief, I'm off to set up the 
contract with Marutomi Commerce.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.310
Right. I'm counting on you.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:17.610
That's a lovely watch.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.470
Oh, it's just a cheap one.

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:20.520
See ya.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:22.580
He always looks so good.

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:25.570
I heard his engagement with the 
director's daughter is going well, too.

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:29.990
This is a nice office you have here...

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:32.090
Y-You guys can't show up at my workplace!

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:33.580
Hey, we're working, too.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:37.510
A cheap watch, huh? 
I'd say it cost around 300,000 yen.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:41.370
I know it's important to look good, 
but you have to pay your debts, too.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:44.220
It'd be wise to have 
your affairs in order...

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.220
or that marriage proposal of 
yours might just fall through.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:50.850
I-I'll pay! I'll pay you, okay?!

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.530
There's still time before my manicure...

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.360
Maybe I'll go shopping for makeup.

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:06.020
The Morikoshi Department Store, please.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.810
I think it's faster to walk there from here.

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:11.040
Shut up and drive!

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:12.860
Wh-Who are you people?!

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:15.440
That's a lot of shopping 
you have there, ma'am.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.840
Might I ask where you got the money for it all?

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:18.880
W-Well...

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:22.130
You haven't made any payments 
in a while, you know.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:24.950
And if you can't manage something soon,

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:27.430
this taxi is going to take you someplace

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:31.140
<i>much</i> farther away than your 
Morikoshi Department Store.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:32.890
I-I'm so sorry!

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:35.390
I'll pay it back! I swear I will!

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:41.400
Dom Peri! Dom Peri!

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:45.080
I always feel the most 
comfortable next to you, Azusa.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:47.380
I can really be myself, you know?

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:48.820
I'm so glad to hear it!

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:50.910
You're perfect in my eyes.

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:54.520
Here's some spending money. 
And let's get another Dom Peri!

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.770
That's another bottle of Dom Pérignon!

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:58.680
Thank you so much!

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.950
Easy money.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:04.710
What the hell are you—

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:08.300
This still doesn't cover it.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:09.810
Uh, well...

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.800
I just need more time!

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.280
Put all of this on 6-3!

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:17.700
I wouldn't, if I were you.

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:18.520
No one asked y—

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:24.600
Your debt just gets bigger, and it's 
because you waste it on crap like this.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:27.180
You know what you could do 
instead of throwing it away?

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.280
R-Right!

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:32.780
It seemed like he had flipped, at first.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.780
Teiai Group

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.900
Going on about how we coerced 
him, how it was illegal...

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:37.030
And the next thing I knew, he started crying.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.330
You didn't push hard enough.

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:44.070
Look, I didn't say I wasn't gonna pay you.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.840
The fact is, you haven't.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:49.400
See, the thing is, that's only because 
the interest has gotten crazy.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:51.530
The interest rate was 
detailed in the contract.

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:54.170
To be honest, I was kinda 
desperate when I got the loan,

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:55.600
so I didn't read it that closely.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.230
Buddy, you'd better not push your luck.

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:01.560
See, there it is! That whole 
intimidation thing. It's just wrong.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:02.960
You really wanna go all the way with this?

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:05.610
Because it's you guys who 
are gonna be in trouble.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:07.770
That's what I thought!

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:10.010
I mean, the interest rates 
you people charge are insane.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:14.390
Look, I can't have you 
showing up here every day.

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:16.380
I'm trying to run a business here.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:19.000
I couldn't care less what you're trying to do.

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:32.840
I want money, not talk.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:43.770
Looks like they finally went 
for the jugular with that guy.

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:46.980
Yeah, and after he was laughing about 
bringing them down the other day.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:50.900
The registry and deed.

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:54.530
You're the boss, right?!

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:55.890
Just give me some more time!

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:57.990
I wanted to pay you back! I swear!

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:02.750
What you want weighs less than 
a single bill of currency.

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:04.490
Let's go.

00:08:04.490 --> 00:08:06.000
Y-Yes, sir.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.300
Damn it, it's society's fault!

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:13.850
If people just gave me some respect...

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:15.510
Shit! Shit!

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:20.520
Damn trash... Does he expect 
society to mother him?

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:30.300
Money matters are life and death matters.
Society isn't your mother.

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:29.110
<i>The maxims of Tonegawa:</i>

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:32.050
<i>"Society isn't your mother."</i>

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:34.010
<i>This is a man who takes 
his own words seriously,</i>

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:36.660
<i>using them to push himself to the next level!</i>

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:40.260
<i>That is Tonegawa Yukio!</i>

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:46.630
<i>The man who survived the carnage of the 
Teiai Group to become its number-two man!</i>

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.850
we're always by your side 
here at Teiai Finance.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:06.850
<b>Finance</b>

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.360
<b><i>Plan responsibly.</i></b>

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.360
Teiai Group

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:16.950
<b>1 Box:
1 Day's Worth
of Vegetables</b>

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:25.280
<i>Tonegawa-sensei, 
the president wants to see you.</i>

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:26.790
Understood.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:30.920
<i>The only hurdle in Tonegawa Yukio's way?</i>

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:36.530
<i>The emperor of the company he works 
at... its dictator, and its tyrant.</i>

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:39.800
<i>The president: Hyoudou Kazutaka!</i>

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:45.060
I'm here, sir—

00:09:48.950 --> 00:09:50.610
Bored.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.320
This is dull. I'm fed up.

00:09:56.130 --> 00:10:00.320
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:00.320
<i>Tonegawa realizes instinctively...</i>

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:00.320
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:04.830
<i>that the next few words out of 
the president's mouth would</i>

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:08.830
<i>open the door to new carnage!</i>

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:11.080
<i>Trapping him in a bottomless bog!</i>

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:16.340
<i>It would mark the descent of death 
itself, opening Hell's gate!</i>

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:20.840
Television, movies, music, it's all a farce.

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:24.960
This pablum about love, romance, 
how we're not alone in the world...

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:27.110
Longing to see someone...

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:31.850
But then not wanting to see them, 
but in the end they do?

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:37.630
"My bangs are too short!" "My jeans are 
too tight!" and all their complaints...

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:40.860
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:10:39.850 --> 00:10:44.110
None of them understands 
what it means to be human.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:46.620
It's a sham. It's a mockery.

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:49.620
I want something authentic.

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:55.380
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:55.380
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:59.710
I want a front row seat to see 
the ugliest side of humanity,

00:10:59.710 --> 00:11:01.110
the most extreme of extremes...

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:06.140
Our true nature: 
destruction, despair, and death.

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:09.890
Now that is true entertainment. Sincere joy.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:15.400
Don't you agree, Tonegawa, my boy?

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:17.650
Yes, I do, sir.

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:20.650
Well, then...

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:24.410
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:24.410
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:28.160
<i>The gate to Hell opens!</i>

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:30.410
That's your new project.

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:34.960
Something to make my flesh 
quake with excitement!

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:40.920
A fight to the death among human filth, 
to energize every cell in my body!

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:44.180
<b>A death game</b>

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:44.180
A death game!

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:49.180
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:49.180
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:55.190
Understood, sir.

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:59.190
<i>Tonegawa is struck out of the blue, 
before the weekend begins!</i>

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:01.220
<i>A trial has arrived!</i>

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:05.450
<i>Despite his status as an executive 
with countless men in his employ,</i>

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:07.260
<i>he is dominated!</i>

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:11.940
<i>Ensuring President Hyoudou's good 
mood always, </i>always<i> takes priority!</i>

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:19.530
<i>He knows this better than anyone, 
because of his status as middle management!</i>

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:23.470
<i>It all falls apart... again!</i>

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:28.360
<i>My weekend golf plans... up in smoke!</i>

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:32.870
<i>This is a tale of the struggles with 
his position and its complications:</i>

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:38.120
<i>Just a small, quaint story of 
the legendary Tonegawa Yukio!</i>

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:49.120
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:49.120
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:13.710
<i>Tonegawa Yukio. The Teiai 
Group's highest ranked manager,</i>

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:16.790
<i>the president's right-hand man.</i>

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:18.290
<b>Meeting Room 3</b>

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:27.620
<i>Under Hyoudou's orders, a new 
project team is gathered.</i>

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:31.390
<i>Men in black are chosen 
from various departments.</i>

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:37.880
<i>This is the first time they will be 
working under Tonegawa directly.</i>

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:40.480
Now, then...

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:43.480
We're initiating a new project.

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:45.400
Failure isn't an option.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:49.010
Our goal is a diabolical diversion, 
a game, to entertain the president.

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:51.490
And the first step is to come up with ideas.

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:53.490
That, however, can wait.

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:56.870
We're starting...

00:14:58.290 --> 00:14:59.620
with introductions!

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:10.810
The whole lot of you look too much alike.

00:15:10.810 --> 00:15:13.640
It's like you were cut from the same 
cloth—not a speck of individuality.

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:16.790
A bunch of men in their 
thirties or thereabouts,

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:19.140
in the same suit, 
wearing the same sunglasses...

00:15:20.470 --> 00:15:22.520
How the hell do I tell you apart?!

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:26.050
Now, granted, those suits 
are standard here at Teiai.

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:28.900
President Hyoudou himself made that call.

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:34.280
That being the case, I can't order 
you to change into casual clothes.

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:37.950
<i>Tonegawa Yukio: The Middle Manager.</i>

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:40.790
Seeing as I can't do that, 
I want introductions.

00:15:41.570 --> 00:15:44.240
Your names, and any hobbies 
or special talents you have.

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:45.040
We'll go down the line.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:47.420
Starting with you.

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:49.900
Get a move on, now.

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:51.680
R-Right!

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:55.180
<i>If I remember right, he used 
to work under the president...</i>

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:58.110
I'm Yamazaki. Yamazaki Kenji.

00:15:58.110 --> 00:16:00.430
My hobby is bowling!

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:03.060
Yamazaki... Yamazaki...

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:06.060
You're Yamazaki. Right, next.

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:08.050
R-Right!

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:09.820
I'm Saemon-saburou Jirou!

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:12.840
<b>Psst...</b>

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:15.590
My hobby is bowling, and...

00:16:15.590 --> 00:16:16.570
Hold on.

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:21.330
That sounded like two people... 
enough names for two people.

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:25.110
Saburou Shiro, like some kind of comedy duo...

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:26.160
Oh, no, sir!

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:27.970
Saemon-saburou is my family name.

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:29.380
<b>Saemon-saburou</b>

00:16:27.860 --> 00:16:29.380
<b>Jirou</b>

00:16:27.970 --> 00:16:29.730
Plus, my name is Jirou.

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:31.340
<b>Saemon-saburou Jirou</b>

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:31.340
Altogether, it's Saemon-saburou Jirou!

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:34.590
<i>What?!</i>

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:38.900
<i>What a pain! It was going to be hard 
enough to remember their names...</i>

00:16:38.900 --> 00:16:40.850
<i>And now this idiot's family 
name is making it worse!</i>

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:45.940
<i>Still, "Saemon-saburou"... 
With a family name that weird,</i>

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:52.390
<i>it should be easy to 
remember him, in particular.</i>

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:55.560
<i>The king of Teiai, President Hyoudou,</i>

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:59.200
<i>would never bother to learn 
the names of his men in black.</i>

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:00.840
All right, you there.

00:17:00.840 --> 00:17:01.850
Sir!

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:06.770
<i>But beneath him, things are different 
for middle manager Tonegawa...</i>

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:10.740
<i>As someone who has to supervise 
and organize these men,</i>

00:17:10.740 --> 00:17:14.470
<i>he can't treat them as broadly 
as the president does.</i>

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:19.750
<i>If anything, he will need their support 
in order to ensure his career goes well.</i>

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:24.980
<i>For Tonegawa, the trust of these men 
in black is a requirement to advance.</i>

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:27.060
<i>Which is why he remembers.</i>

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:31.170
<i>He holds his tongue, and remembers the 
confusing names of these men in black.</i>

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:34.640
<i>Tonegawa Yukio: the middle manager.</i>

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:34.640
Saemon-saburou... Saemon-saburou...

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:35.240
Next!

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:39.630
Kawasaki Toshimasa! My hobby is bowling!

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:41.240
It's a pleasure to work under you, sir!

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:43.400
<i>Kawasaki, Kawasaki...</i>

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:46.170
<i>Well, at least his name is normal enough.</i>

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:47.750
<i>No, wait!</i>

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:48.790
<i>This is bad!</i>

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:50.500
<b>Kawasaki</b>

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:51.890
<i>Kawasaki is bad! 
The first one's name was Yamazaki!</i>

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.550
<b>Kawasaki</b>

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:52.570
<b>Yamazaki</b>

00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:54.010
<i>Their names end the same way!</i>

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:56.700
<i>What a pain in the ass!</i>

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:59.880
<i>It's possible that if he hadn't 
noticed the similarity,</i>

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:02.410
<i>he may have been able to 
memorize both with ease.</i>

00:18:02.410 --> 00:18:06.640
<i>But because he noticed... he struggles!</i>

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:14.010
<i>And Tonegawa noticed! 
It's only natural that he would!</i>

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:15.150
<i>That's because...</i>

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:19.160
<i>He is a winner, and observations 
like that are what have allowed him</i>

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:21.430
<i>to come out on top so many times before!</i>

00:18:21.430 --> 00:18:23.160
<i>A realization made because he's exceptional!</i>

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.040
Next!

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:25.410
Y-Yes, sir!

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:28.160
<i>Come on, have an 
easy-to-remember family name...</i>

00:18:29.130 --> 00:18:31.670
<i>Tonegawa wishes. And then...</i>

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:35.670
Ogino... Ogino Keiichi. My hobby is bowling.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:36.670
All right!

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:38.280
<i>Surely this is divine providence!</i>

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:40.630
Ogino. You're Ogino, then, right?

00:18:40.630 --> 00:18:41.680
Yes, sir...

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.300
Very good.

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:46.620
<i>An Ogino, at a time like this!</i>

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:49.220
<i>What a windfall! 
It's a ray of hope shining down!</i>

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:50.440
All right, next.

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:52.770
<b>Psst...</b>

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:54.840
<i>What was that?!</i>

00:18:54.840 --> 00:19:03.950
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:18:55.830 --> 00:19:00.290
<i>Suddenly, an inexplicable 
dread seizes Tonegawa.</i>

00:18:57.000 --> 00:19:03.950
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:03.950
<i>He doesn't know what it is... but...</i>

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:08.960
<i>It's an unpleasant premonition, 
like something coiling around his neck...</i>

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:11.960
I-Is something wrong, Tonegawa-sensei?

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:15.460
N-No, it's nothing. Next man, you're up.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:18.410
<i>I must be imagining it. I have to be.</i>

00:19:18.410 --> 00:19:22.970
<i>But soon, the reason for his 
ominous dread will become obvious.</i>

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:25.720
I'm Hagio. Hagio Junichi.

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:30.850
My hobby is bowl—

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:32.520
<b>Hagino</b>

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:34.680
Hagino and Ogio!

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:33.980
<b>Hagino</b>

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:33.980
<b>Ogio</b>

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:36.360
This can't be a coincidence!

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:38.740
T-Tonegawa-sensei...

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:39.760
It's the other way around.

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:41.450
Ogino and Hagio.

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:42.240
<b>Ogino</b>

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:42.240
<b>Hagio</b>

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:45.730
<i>Tonegawa hits his limit! His wall!</i>

00:19:45.730 --> 00:19:47.640
<i>And something's about to crumble!</i>

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:50.500
<i>He can hear it within himself!</i>

00:19:52.130 --> 00:19:53.960
What difference does it make, damn it?!

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:57.490
I've had enough! 
You're all getting name changes!

00:19:57.490 --> 00:19:59.960
I'm giving you names I can remember!

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:03.330
And not just your names! Your hobbies!

00:20:03.330 --> 00:20:06.490
Every last one of you is into bowling?!

00:20:06.490 --> 00:20:08.140
What are you, teenagers?!

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:11.030
Or were you all born in some 
kind of bowling village?!

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:12.810
Here we are. You're "Gutter Balls."

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:15.560
Every last one of you will 
now be known as Gutter Ball!

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:20.190
And your scores are all zero!

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:23.320
Isn't one of you capable of a strike?!

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:26.570
Can't one of you throw a strike 
into my memory?! Into my brain?!

00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:29.830
Strike!

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:32.250
Damn it, Kawasaki, say something!

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:33.350
It's Yamazaki, sir.

00:20:35.110 --> 00:20:38.470
<i>This meeting would ultimately end 
after a lot of incoherent babble,</i>

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:41.290
<i>finishing with absolutely no progress.</i>

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:43.130
<i>Too bad, Tonegawa.</i>

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:44.630
<b>Meeting Room 3</b>

00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:46.270
Gutter Balls, huh?

00:20:46.270 --> 00:20:48.090
Tonegawa-sensei was really pissed.

00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:48.830
This is bad.

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:49.440
Yeah.

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:50.150
Seriously!

00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:52.890
All right, let's go bowling!

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:54.330
Might as well.

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:56.400
Maybe I can manage an all-spare game.

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:01.900
<i>He didn't have much luck 
with his subordinates.</i>

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:04.180
<i>But hang in there, Tonegawa!</i>

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:06.410
<i>Don't give up, Tonegawa!</i>

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:11.720
<i>This is the story of a lone 
man who struggles as</i>

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:15.580
<i>an employer to his employees, 
the men in black...</i>

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:20.090
<i>Tonegawa Yukio: Middle Manager!</i>

00:22:54.580 --> 00:22:56.570
<i>Next time: "Conjecture."</i>

00:22:55.580 --> 00:23:01.000
<b>Conjecture</b>
